## Service Files

**Primary** (`/etc/systemd/system/anvil-rope.service` on rope-vps):
- `--host 127.0.0.1` (localhost only, Rope node wraps it on :8545)
- `MemoryMax=50G`
- `TimeoutStopSec=300` — 5 min graceful shutdown
- `KillMode=mixed` — SIGTERM to main, SIGKILL to remaining after timeout
- `ExecStartPre=/opt/datachain-rope/scripts/validate-anvil-state.sh` — state integrity check
- `ExecStartPost=/opt/datachain-rope/scripts/anvil-post-start.sh` — restores DNAT rule + waits for Anvil responsive
- `ExecStop=/opt/datachain-rope/scripts/anvil-safe-stop.sh` — removes DNAT, flushes conntrack, then takes RPC dump
- `StartLimitIntervalSec=600` + `StartLimitBurst=5` (in [Unit]) — max 5 restarts per 10 min

**Secondary** (`/etc/systemd/system/anvil-rope.service` on anvil-vps):
- `--host 0.0.0.0` (accepts remote connections for failover)
- `MemoryMax=50G`

## Protection Scripts

| Script | Path | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| **validate-anvil-state.sh** | `/opt/datachain-rope/scripts/validate-anvil-state.sh` | Runs before Anvil starts. Checks `state.json` ends with `}`. If corrupted: moves aside, tries backup `.gz`, then SCP from secondary. Falls through to fresh start if all fail. |
| **anvil-safe-stop.sh** | `/opt/datachain-rope/scripts/anvil-safe-stop.sh` | Runs before Anvil stops. **First** removes DNAT rule + flushes conntrack (instant failover). **Then** takes `anvil_dumpState` RPC snapshot as `prestop-*.hex.gz`. |
| **anvil-post-start.sh** | `/opt/datachain-rope/scripts/anvil-post-start.sh` | Runs after Anvil starts. Restores DNAT rule, enables `route_localnet`, waits up to 60s for Anvil to become responsive before declaring ready. |
| **dcrope-watchdog.sh** | `/home/ubuntu/dcrope-watchdog.sh` | Runs every 5 min via cron. v5: RPC timeout = **log only** (never restart); only restarts on `failed`/`inactive` state; ignores `activating`/`deactivating`; 15-min cooldown. |
| **anvil-state-backup.sh** | `/opt/datachain-rope/scripts/anvil-state-backup.sh` | Runs every 15 min via cron. Takes `anvil_dumpState` from port **8595** (direct) + gzip copy of `state.json`. Keeps 10 most recent of each type. |

